Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_dirwrite.c
Line: 1297
Function: TIFFWriteDirectorySec
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: dirsize is computed in 64-bit as 2 + ndir*12 + 4 (classic) or 8 + ndir*20 + 8 (BigTIFF) and passed to _TIFFmallocExt(tif, dirsize). On 32-bit builds, the implicit conversion to tmsize_t can truncate a large dirsize, causing an undersized allocation. The subsequent loop starting at line 1309 (or 1345 for BigTIFF) writes dirsize bytes into dirmem, resulting in a heap buffer overflow (CWE-122) due to the prior integer truncation.

Source context:
```c
     1257:          */
     1258:         tif->tif_dataoff = tif->tif_diroff + dirsize;
     1259:         if (!(tif->tif_flags & TIFF_BIGTIFF))
     1260:             tif->tif_dataoff = (uint32_t)tif->tif_dataoff;
     1261:         if ((tif->tif_dataoff < tif->tif_diroff) ||
     1262:             (tif->tif_dataoff < (uint64_t)dirsize))
     1263:         {
     1264:             TIFFErrorExtR(tif, module, "Maximum TIFF file size exceeded");
     1265:             goto bad;
     1266:         }
     1267:         if (tif->tif_dataoff & 1)
     1268:             tif->tif_dataoff++;
     1269:     } /* while() */
     1270:     if (isimage)
     1271:     {
